Z||000000||Lynx||05-13-99||02:23 AM||||Ok i was reading a earler posting about there being 3 different spring tensions on a Fiero. When i bought my Fiero the person put a spoiler on it but the lid springs are so bad it dosent even act like there are springs at all. Well one person said you can simply adjust them for more tension, is this true and if it is how do i do it.<p>P.S. My head has a knot on the back of it because i knocked over the prop rod when i was working on it and the DAMN thing hit me
Z||000001||Phil||05-13-99||05:46 AM||||One end of the spring is hooked over a pin on a bracket on the fire wall. This bracket has 3 or 4 holes, just move the pins to get more initial torque on the spring. Sounds easy but it can be a bear.
Z||000002||theogre||05-13-99||07:01 AM||||if that's still not enough, try rodney dickman's add on gas tube kit. looks nice, not too expensive, much easier then changing out the springs.<p>I don't have the link handy.<p>Be very carefull adjusting the springs. they can hurt you badly if they get away from you.
